# ============================================
# KUBAPP DATABASE
# ============================================

# Deployment environment
ENV="dev"

# Database deployment mode
# local = database lives in KUBAPP account
# cross = database lives in separate database account
DATABASE_MODE="local"


# ============================================
# AWS ACCOUNTS
# ============================================

# KUBAPP AWS account
KUBAPP_ACCOUNT_ID="111111222222222233333333344444"

# AWS account where the cross-account database
# infrastructure will be provisioned
DATABASE_ACCOUNT_ID="5555555666666777777888888999"


# ============================================
# AWS PROFILES
# ============================================

# AWS profile used when database resources
# are provisioned in the KUBAPP account
PROFILE_LOCAL=""

# AWS profile used when database resources
# are provisioned in the separate database account
PROFILE_CROSS=""


# ============================================
# AWS REGION
# ============================================

REGION="us-east-1"

### What each value means

```text
DATABASE_MODE
    │
    ├── local
    │     └── STATE_ACCOUNT_ID = KUBAPP_ACCOUNT_ID
    │
    └── cross
          └── STATE_ACCOUNT_ID = DATABASE_ACCOUNT_ID
```

The profiles follow the same selection:

```text
local  → PROFILE_LOCAL
cross  → PROFILE_CROSS
```

And the state location is then derived automatically:

```text
local:
kubapp-database-tf-state-4535627282881927364449448
dev/database/tf-state

cross:
kubapp-database-tf-state-${DATABASE_ACCOUNT_ID}
dev/database/tf-state

